senses.gloss:
1 मह् महते महयति महते महय˚ते pp. महित
(q.v.) A. (M.) gladden;
 delight, exalt, refresh, excite, impel;
 esteem
highly, honour;
 M. be glad, rejoice at (instr. or acc.);
 grant, bestow.
— सम् stir up, excite;
 honour, celebrate.

2 म॑ह् (f. म॑ह् & मही॑) great, mighty, powerful, strong,
abundant;
 old, aged. f. मही॑ the earth (as the great one), ground,
soil, land, country, kingdom;
 space;
 host;
 cow;
 du. heaven and earth;
pl. rivers, waters.

2 मह॑ a. great, rich, abundant, abstr. ˚ता† f.;
 n. pl.
great deeds.

महत्तम (superl.) very great or high;
 m. an eminent
man.

मह॑न्त् (महा॑न्त्, f. महती॑;
 ˚— mostly महा q.v.)
great (in all mgs, i.e.) big, large, tall;
 extensive, long, protracted,
far advanced;
 much, many, abundant, numerous;
 intensive, thick, dense;
mighty, important, high, noble, distinguished, eminent. — m. a great or
noble man, (±आत्मन्) the intellect;
 n. anything great or important;
greatness, might.

महाकाल m. a form and a temple of Śiva;
 f. ई a form
of Durgā.

2 महागुण a. possessing great qualities or merits,
distinguished;
 abstr. ˚त्व n.

महाजन m. a great or eminent man (also coll.);
 a great
number of men, people (also pl.).

महातपस् a. much afflicted or doing severe penance;
 m.
N. of a sage.

महातेजस् a. possessing great fire or lustre;
 glorious,
mighty.

महादेव॑ m. the great god, esp. Rudra-Śiva or Viṣṇu;
f. ई the great goddess i.e. Pārvatī or Lakṣmī, the first wife of a
king.

2 महाधन a. having or costing much money;
 rich,
wealthy, costly, precious.

महानग्न॑ m. lover or athlete;
 f. आ & ई whore (lit.
quite naked).

महानद m. a great river or stream;
 f. ई the same, E.
of Gaṅgā.

महानुभाव a. high-potent or magnanimous;
 abstr.
˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

महापार्श्व a. broad-sided (leech);
 m. N. of a Dānava &
a Rākṣasa.

महापुण्य a. very auspicious or fortunate;
 very good,
pure, or holy.

महाप्रभ a. very resplendent;
 f. ˚प्रभा great
brightness.

महाभय n. great danger or dread;
 a. very dangerous or
dreadful.

महाभारत s. (±आहव or युद्ध) the great war of
the Bharatas;
 n. (±आख्यान) the great narrative of the war of the Bh.

महाभूत a. (being) great;
 m. great creature or being;
n. grosser element (ph.).

2 महाभोग a. having great windings or coils (also
˚वन्त् or ˚भोगिन्);
 m. a serpent.

महामात्र a. great (in measure), best, first of (—˚)
—m. great man, high official, minister;
 elephant-driver or keeper.

महामाय a. very deceitful or illusory;
 m. E. of sev.
gods, f. आ & ई E. of Durgā.

महारव m. loud sound or cry;
 a. loud-sounding, crying,
roaring.

महाराष्ट्र m. pl. the Mahrattas;
 f. ई the language of
the M.

माहाराष्ट्र f. ई belonging to the Mahrattas;
 f. ई
the M. language.

महार्थ m. great thing, important matter;
 adj. great,
important, wealthy.

महाविक्रम a. having great might or courage;
 m. N. of
lion.

2 महासत्त्व a. great-minded, noble, virtuous,
courageous;
 abstr. ˚ता f.

महासाधु a. very good, excellent;
 f. ˚साध्वी =
महासती.

महा॑सेन a. having a great army;
 E. of Skanda, N. of
sev. kings.

1 महाहवि॑स् n. chief oblation or clarified butter;
 E. of
Śiva.

म॑हि adj. (only ˚— & nom. acc. sgl.) great;
 adv. greatly,
much.

महिम॑न् m. greatness, might, majesty;
 instr. also as adv.
greatly, mightily.

महीय् मही˚य॑ते be great, happy, or blessed;
 be exalted
or honoured by (gen.).

माहेन्द्र॑ f. ई great Indra's eastern;
 w. धनुस् n.
rainbow.

महेश्वर m. = prec., also E. of sev. other gods, esp.
of the 4 world-protectors;
 f. ई E. of Durgā.
